  "id": "concrete-operation",
  "term": "concrete operation",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, a concrete operation is the actual, conscious act of thinking as it occurs in a particular person, rather than thought considered only in the abstract. It refers to the subjective mental process itself in its relation to an object.",
